  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 228 AM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nThe front will battle the heat on Sunday and could remain nearly\nstationary across far northern Oklahoma much of the day, with\nmedium-high probabilities of rain/storms expanding and shifting\nsouthward into portions of central Oklahoma by Sunday evening.\nThis will likely keep hot temperatures for the majority of the CWA\non Sunday. As the cooler airmass begins to advect into Oklahoma \nSunday afternoon and evening, low-level frontogenesis sharpens and\nmid-level lapse rates steepen. As a result, strong to severe \nstorms with large hail are possible by Sunday afternoon/evening \nacross northern Oklahoma. \n\nThe front moves slowly southward on Sunday night and Monday morning,\nand may not fully exit our area until late Monday. There is the\nhope that Monday will mark the end to our long season of triple-\ndigit temperatures as highs remain in the 80's and 90's, with \ncontinued shower and storm chances. \n\nThompson",
